# Extension Policy Manager - User Guide

This guide describes how to open, authorize, and use the **Extension Policy Manager** web interface to manage your organization's browser extension whitelist and blacklist rules.

---

## 1. How to Launch the Webpage

To open the application:
1. Locate your project folder (e.g., `jsonformatterproject`).
2. Double-click the **`index.html`** file located inside the folder, or drag-and-drop it into any modern web browser (like Google Chrome, Microsoft Edge, or Mozilla Firefox).

---

## 2. Linking and Authorizing the Target File (`policy.json`)

When you launch the page, it runs locally in your browser. Before you can save any changes, you must connect it to your local configuration file. 

Depending on whether this is your first time opening the app or a returning session, follow the appropriate scenario below:

### Scenario A: First-Time Use (File Not Linked)
If you are opening the app for the first time or if the connection has been reset:
1. The status indicator in the top-right corner will show **Local Sandbox (Unlinked)**.
2. A brown banner at the top of the page will say: **"Not linked to a local policy file. Changes will only save in browser memory."**
3. Click the **"Link policy.json"** button on the right side of the banner.
4. Select your local `policy.json` file from the folder picker.

```text
========================================================================
[ PLACEHOLDER: Insert Screenshot A (Unlinked Banner & Link policy.json Button) ]
========================================================================
```

---

### Scenario B: Returning Session (File Already Attached/Linked)
If the browser remembers the linked file from a previous session, the app automatically bypasses the linking stage:
1. The app will **not** ask you to link the `policy.json` file again.
2. The status indicator in the top-right corner will show **Awaiting Authorization**.
3. The brown banner at the top of the page will automatically say: **"Linked to: policy.json. Click button to authorize writing."**
4. Click the **"Authorize Write"** button on the right side of the banner.
5. Your browser will show a security prompt (e.g., *"Allow this site to edit files?"* or *"View files"*). Click **Allow** or **Save Changes** to grant the app permission to write changes.
6. The status indicator in the top-right corner will change to **Authorized**.

